Compaq is pleased to announce the field test of their latest Developers'

Toolkit Supplement for Tru64 UNIX.  The field test is free and open to
all
developers.  The kit can be downloaded from

    http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/dtk/

This new version of the DTK Supplement will install and run on Tru64
UNIX
versions V4.0D, V4.0F, V4.0G, V5.0, and V5.0A and contains
new-and-improved
versions of the following development tools

    Compaq C -- a standards-compliant, full-featured, highly optimizing
    compiler specifically developed to exploit the 64-bit Alpha
architecture

    Spike -- a newly developed post-link optimizer that is particularly
    effective when utilizing application profile information

    Visual Threads -- a debugging and analysis tool for multi-threaded
    applications that helps users detect deadlock, thread usage errors,
    shared data protection problems, and poor performance

    Ladebug -- a powerful, multi-language, source-level debugger

    Program Analysis Tools -- a suite of debugging and profiling tools
that
    includes third (for memory leak detection), hiprof (a hierarchical
    instruction profiler), and pixie (to instrument an application with
    profiling code)

    Graphical Program Analysis Tools -- a graphical user interface for
the
    program analysis tools

The field test is expected to last until the official product is
released
in July.  Field test customers are invited to send feedback via the
website.





