Hi all,

We are using OrbixMT 2.3c on Digital Unix 4.0F.
When one of our CORBA servers dies abnormally,
"psit" still lists it as an active server and we
cannot restart it.

We did a trace of the system calls on orbixd and found
that on the termination of our server process, orbixd
does not wake up immediately from select(2) even though
the connection to the server is broken. By the way there
is always a connection between the server and the orbixd
which is closed on server termination. When it eventually
does, it does a read(2) which returns 0 and subsequently
the entry in "psit" goes away.

This behaviour does not occur on 4.0D OS. I am not sure
if we need to install some patches to get around this.

Any help in this regard is appreciated.

raj...


